        "mission_intent": "Subject: Full Specification Needed for PCAOB Standards Adoption and Advisory Group Governance Framework\n\nWe need a comprehensive specification document covering the Board's authority and procedures for adopting auditing, quality control, ethics, and independence standards as outlined under the Sarbanes-Oxley Act. The spec should address the full lifecycle: initial adoption or amendment of standards (including the ability to amend, modify, or repeal existing professional group statements in whole or in part), the process for establishing initial and transitional standards prior to the SEC's determination under Section 101(d), and the requirement that such transitional standards receive separate Commission approval outside the normal Section 107 rulemaking procedures. Additionally, the document must detail the governance framework for expert advisory groups that the Board or its staff may convene, including composition requirements\u2014practicing accountants, other subject-matter experts, and representatives of interested groups\u2014along with conflict-of-interest rules the Board must prescribe for advisory group participants. The spec should map each procedural step to the relevant statutory section, identify which approvals are Commission-dependent versus Board-discretionary, and ensure the framework can be implemented in our compliance tracking system by the end of Q3. Please coordinate with Legal and the External Audit Liaison team for review before finalizing.",
